course: dictionary
lesson: 8789
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word shang does not come from English. It is a Chinese word, and one spelling can have several meanings. Context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it and ask what would fit best.
explain: «Shang kings, over 3,000 years ago, asked their ancestors questions by heating bones and shells.» Kings and ancient times are the clues here, so Shang means a ruling family, called a dynasty. In an English text, the names of people or places often work the same way.
explain: In Mandarin, «shàng» means up, on or above, and «shàng xué» means go to school. The little mark over the a is a tone, and it changes how the word sounds. You cannot always hear the tone from a page, so the sentence is your best clue.
fact: Shang was an early dynasty, or ruling family, of ancient China.
fact: The Shang are famous for their bronze work and for writing on oracle bones.
fact: Shang kings heated bones and shells until they cracked, then read the cracks as answers from their ancestors.
fact: In Mandarin, «shàng» means up, on or above, and «to go to», as in «shàng xué».
fact: Shang is also a Chinese surname and a given name, and «Shànghǎi» means on the sea.
exercise: «Shang kings, over 3,000 years ago, asked their ancestors questions by heating bones and shells.» In this sentence, what is Shang? | A modern city on the sea | A Mandarin word meaning up | A word meaning last month | *A ruling family of ancient China
exercise: In Mandarin, «shàng xué» means what? | Last month | On the sea | Go to sleep | *Go to school
exercise: «Shànghǎi» is a city name. What does it mean? | *On the sea | A bronze bowl | Last month | Ancient castle
test: «The Shang dynasty carved questions on turtle shells and ox bones.» What did the Shang carve their questions on? | Paper | Leaves | *Turtle shells and ox bones | Glass
test: Shang is also a name. How is it used? | As a Chinese dish | *As a Chinese surname and given name | As a bronze sword | As a type of dog
exam: Lin reads «shàng ge yuè» and thinks it means next month. What does it really mean? | *Last month | Next month | Go to school | Up the hill
